---
// A returning visitor's single line, shown while the shell mounts, with no minimum or
// maximum duration. Shares `BootScreen`'s full-viewport black ground and CRT classes;
// `shell.css` shows it only while `html.restore` is set and hides it once
// `html.shell-ready` is set. `aria-hidden` throughout: the island makes the single
// desktop-ready announcement.
//
// `#restore-line` starts with the zero-windows wording so a skip during a first boot,
// which shows this element without passing `HeadGate`'s restore branch, still reads as a
// sensible line. `HeadGate.astro`'s script overwrites the text on an actual restore.
---

<div id="restore" class="scan" aria-hidden="true">
  <p id="restore-line" class="bloom">
    RESUME &middot; DESKTOP RESTORED
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  #restore {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 2;
    background: #000;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* Slashed zero: chrome/log output, not body copy. */
    font-feature-settings: 'zero';
  }

  #restore-line {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
